## Domain
Quantum bigraphs: the link graph IS the entanglement graph; a composite is the
entanglement scope (holds the joint amplitude); `tensor`/`divide` are the join/split
duality (`docs/quantum-bigraphs.md`). The substrate is **std**: `meta::handle` (effects),
`meta::sample` (Born-rule measurement), `meta::tensor` / `meta::factorize`, and the `Qubits`
type with `.cnot` / `.tensor` / `.factorize` / `.separable` methods. Surface:
`packages/quantum/` (19 demos, pure-`.ys`). Adjacent: `core` / `lang` (substrate + surface),
`mesh` (quantum over a mesh link — M3/M4), `unify` (the shared `Complex` / `Signal[ℂ]` sort,
#64/#68; the M4 one-engine).

## Identity — the †-compact prop
Every domain is a presented theory; quantum is the **dagger-compact prop** — unitary
ℂ-linear maps; cups/caps = entanglement (a Bell pair is a cup); the dagger = adjoint /
measurement. `fold`/`unfurl` = the compact cup/cap = entanglement = the same maneuver
distribution uses. Quantum shares the `Complex` sort with manifold (quantum = unitary,
manifold = dissipative; one ℂ-linear category, Selinger CPM). The library should make this
structure first-class: gates as morphisms, circuits as composition, the bigraph as wiring.

## Now / next
**Vision (human, 2026-06-11):** make quantum a RICH, USEFUL, GENERAL tool — canonical
types + gates + registers + circuits + measurement as composable primitives to explore ANY
quantum system, fully working across LOCAL / STREAM / MESH modes. Generalize from the
bespoke demos (bell / ghz / teleportation) to a LIBRARY (a gate set + a circuit
abstraction; e.g. Bell = `H ; CNOT` built from library gates, not a hand-rolled amplitude).

