## Done
- **Distributed #2 — LOCC's classical channel over a `mesh:` link (the first distributed quantum
  demo; grand-synthesis M2).** 2026-06-12. Two `.ys` peers (`locc-alice.ys`, `locc-bob.ys`) each
  declare a CRDT-safe `link channel :: map[String] mesh`. Alice measures her |+> and writes the
  outcome to HER key; ONE gossip round (the mesh M1 runtime — `MeshReplica`/`gossip`/`mesh_links`,
  REUSED not cloned) replicates the classical String to Bob, who reads it and prepares |bit>. ONLY
  the classical bit crosses — the quantum stays local (entanglement never split, §VI).
  `tests/quantum_locc_mesh.rs` drives the gossip (uses `compile_with_core(std_core())` so the
  `Qubits` methods are present — a bare `compile()` core has the type but not the methods). 39
  quantum suite green.
- **Q5 measurement-with-collapse + clean re-expressions + phase estimation.** 2026-06-12.
  `observe(qubit, seed)` — projective single-qubit measurement that COLLAPSES + renormalizes,
  returning `{outcome, state, prob}` (`quantum.rs`; `quantum-measure.ys` shows a Bell partner
  collapsing). With it, the Q5-blocked protocols re-expressed CLEAN (gate methods + observe, no
  hand-rolled amplitudes): **teleportation** (`quantum-teleportation.ys` — fidelity 1.0, Bob
  reconstructs |ψ> via observe-collapse + conditional Z/X; test now fidelity-based) and **LOCC**
  (`quantum-locc.ys` — `alice_bit == bob_bit`, eval-time). Plus **phase estimation**
  (`quantum-phase-estimation.ys` — 2-qubit QPE of U=S reads φ=1/4 as '01' exactly; the
  measurement-extracts-a-phase core of Shor). 14 quantum lib + 38 suite green. (Build broke
  mid-turn on lang's in-flight `Def::Functor` — flagged; lang fixed it; recovered.)
- **Superdense coding (#12) — the explorations capstone.** 2026-06-12. Send 2 classical bits with
  ONE transmitted qubit: Alice Pauli-encodes (00→I, 01→X, 10→Z, 11→XZ) onto her half of a
  pre-shared Bell pair; Bob Bell-measures `[cnot, h]` and recovers both bits with P=1.
  `packages/quantum/ys/quantum-superdense.ys` — **ZERO new Rust primitive** (h/x/z/cnot + `prob`):
  the tool is now expressive enough that a real protocol is pure `.ys`. All 4 messages recovered
  exactly. 36 suite green. **EXPLORATIONS DONE: CHSH + Deutsch–Jozsa + Grover + QFT + superdense**
  (BB84 = optional tail — random bases + sifting).
- **QFT — the Quantum Fourier Transform (#12).** 2026-06-12. The quantum DFT (heart of Shor /
  phase estimation). Needed one key-permutation primitive — `swap` — plus the `cphase` from Grover.
  `packages/quantum/ys/quantum-qft.ys` (3-qubit): H + controlled-phase rotations + a bit-reversal
  swap. Verified: QFT|000⟩ = uniform (P=1/8), and QFT⁻¹∘QFT = identity (round-trip = 1.0). **The
  first algorithm with genuinely COMPLEX amplitudes** — `qft_001` shows the `e^(2πik/8)` phases as
  `[re,im]` (i/√8, etc.) — the payoff for the shared `Complex` substrate (#68). 13 quantum lib + 35
  suite green.
- **Controlled gates (CZ / controlled-phase) + Grover's search (#12).** 2026-06-12. One new
  primitive — `apply_controlled_1q(state, c, t, U)`, the generalization of CNOT (a controlled
  single-qubit unitary) — gives `cz` + `cphase` (the QFT gate) as methods + circuit constructors +
  `apply_gate_spec` ops. `packages/quantum/ys/quantum-grover.ys`: 2-qubit Grover (oracle =
  phase-flip |w⟩ via `cz`/`x`; diffusion = inversion about the mean) finds the marked item with
  CERTAINTY (P=1) in ONE iteration, for three different marks — pure `.ys`. 12 quantum lib + 34
  suite (incl the Grover behavior test) green.
- **Deutsch–Jozsa — the second exploration (#12).** 2026-06-12. Decides f:{0,1}ⁿ→{0,1} CONSTANT
  vs BALANCED in ONE quantum query (classically up to 2ⁿ⁻¹+1). The algorithm is PURE `.ys`
  (`packages/quantum/ys/quantum-deutsch-jozsa.ys`: H + X + CNOT oracles + the circuit + phase
  kickback); it needed ONE new PRIMITIVE — `Qubits.prob(pattern)`, the marginal measurement
  probability `Σ|amp|²` over basis keys matching a `*`-wildcard pattern (`prob('00*')`). The
  boundary working as designed: a new algorithm = `.ys` + at most one instantly-`.ys`-callable
  primitive. const → P(00)=1, balanced → 0 (exact). 11 quantum lib + 33 suite (incl the DJ
  behavior test in `quantum_examples.rs`) green.
- **Full `.ys` parity — the demos re-expressed on the gate layer (#13).** 2026-06-12. Deleted the
  redundant hand-rollers (`quantum-bell-state`, `quantum-ghz` — `quantum-circuit.ys` covers them).
  Re-expressed the distinct ones to the canonical `Qubits` methods: `quantum-engine` /
  `-engine-measure` (gates as engine PROCESSES — `state.hadamard(0)` / `.cnot(0,1)` /
  `.measure(seed)`; intermediate slots need a tagged-Qubits placeholder `def empty :: Qubits`
  since gate dispatch keys off the `_type` tag, and a bare body-literal map is untagged),
  `quantum-bell-measure` (Bell from gates + `.measure`), `quantum-two-bells` (FLATTENED to two
  independent `Qubits` registers — the nested-composite output surfacing was fragile + untested).
  KEPT: `interference` / `effects-handle` (algebraic-effects demos — a different capability);
  `teleportation` / `locc` stay hand-rolled because they need **measurement-with-collapse +
  conditional correction** (Q5 / slice-9) — they are the CONSUMERS that motivate Q5 (the
  boundary's "add the missing primitive" signal, not laziness). README updated. 32 suite green.
- **The Rust↔`.ys` boundary + `.ys` examples as the tested source of truth.** 2026-06-11.
  Settled the boundary ([[feedback_rust_ys_boundary]]): Rust = PRIMITIVES (type+algebra, hot
  kernels, irreducible ops — each INSTANTLY `.ys`-callable on registration); `.ys` = COMPOSITIONS
  (circuits, algorithms, protocols, ALL examples). Applied it: new `quantum-duality.ys` (complex
  tensor/factorize round-trip + entanglement detection, proven through `.ys` — the i-phase factor
  is recovered) + `crates/chrysalis/tests/quantum_examples.rs`, a behavior harness that RUNS the
  new demos (chsh/circuit/gates/duality) and asserts golden VALUES (CHSH S>2 = 2√2, Bell
  amplitudes, S²=Z, separable flags). REMOVED the Rust CHSH reimplementation — the algorithm IS
  `quantum-chsh.ys`; Rust keeps only a `correlation` PRIMITIVE test. 10 quantum lib (primitives) +
  32 suite (incl 4 `.ys` behavior tests) green. *Remaining parity (#13): re-express the
  hand-rolling demos.*
- **CHSH / Bell inequality — the first exploration (#12).** 2026-06-11. A circuit-level PROOF
  that entanglement ≠ classical correlation. New `Qubits.correlation()` = ⟨Z⊗Z⊗…⟩ (parity
  expectation `Σ|amp|²·(-1)^popcount`). Measure a Bell pair at the optimal CHSH angles
  (Alice {0, π/2}, Bob {π/4, -π/4}) by rotating each axis with `ry(q, -θ)` then reading the
  correlator: **S = 2.8284271 = 2√2**, exceeding the classical bound 2 (Tsirelson). Rust test
  `chsh_exceeds_the_classical_bound` (exact to 1e-9) + `packages/quantum/ys/quantum-chsh.ys`
  (10 quantum lib tests; 28 suite green). *Next exploration: Deutsch–Jozsa / Grover (need a
  CZ / controlled-phase 2-qubit gate — the gate set's next addition), then QFT (rides ℂ).*
- **Complex `tensor`/`factorize` + the Circuit abstraction.** 2026-06-11.
  **Correctness (#10):** `prelude::tensor` now ℂ-multiplies amplitudes; `prelude::factorize`
  generalized to rank-1 over ℂ (the real ± sign became a per-row complex PHASE) + a new
  `complex::div`. Reduces EXACTLY to the real algorithm for real inputs (the 28 tests
  unchanged). Proven: (i|1⟩)⊗|0⟩ factorizes + round-trips; (|00⟩+i|11⟩)/√2 is correctly NOT
  separable. **Circuit abstraction (#11, the "tool"):** a circuit = a LIST of gate specs
  (`{op, qubits, params}` — transparent DATA); `Qubits.run(circuit)` folds them in ONE tick
  (`apply_gate_spec` interpreter in `quantum.rs`; unknown op errors loudly). Surface
  constructors in `packages/quantum/ys/circuit.ys` (h/x/y/z/s/t/cnot/phase/rx/ry/rz). Demo
  `quantum-circuit.ys`: **Bell = `[h(0), cnot(0,1)]`, GHZ = `[h(0), cnot(0,1), cnot(1,2)]`**
  as compositions (not hand-rolled), + `H;S;H` carrying complex amplitudes through a circuit.
  9 quantum lib tests + 28 suite green.
- **Complex amplitudes — the foundational unlock (#68; human-prioritized).** 2026-06-11.
  The shared **`Complex` sort** in `crates/prism-std/src/complex.rs` (per categorical-core
  §6b: `array[[2]]` re/im; `add/sub/mul/scale/neg/conj/abs/abs2/arg/from_phase/rotate`;
  **float→complex coercion + exact-real collapse** — the migration hinge) — 6 lib tests
  (i²=−1, |3+4i|=5, from_phase). `Qubits` migrated `map[float] → complex amplitudes` with the
