  general `apply_1q(state, q, U)` + a 2×2 matrix per gate (the gate-library-as-data seam) —
  6 gate unit tests. `measure` now uses `|amp|²`. Backward-compat is EXACT (a bare float is
  `re+0i`; an exactly-real result collapses to a bare float), so the **28 quantum integration
  tests stay green**. `Complex` registered into the Core (`compile.rs` →
  `prism_std::register_complex_type`). New `packages/quantum/ys/quantum-gates.ys`
  (auto-covered by the smoke sweep) shows S|1⟩=i|1⟩, Y|0⟩=i|1⟩, T|1⟩=e^{iπ/4}, S²=Z, and
  **Bell = `H;CNOT` composed from library gates** (no hand-rolled amplitudes). Total: **40
